# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hosted free analyses. All three must be set for a visitor without their own
# API key to run anything. Leave them unset and the app still works — it just
# runs in bring-your-own-key mode and reports HOSTED_UNAVAILABLE honestly
# rather than pretending a visitor spent an allowance they never had.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The provider key that serves free hosted analyses.
#
# SET A SPEND LIMIT ON THIS KEY IN THE PROVIDER CONSOLE. That limit — not any
# code in this repository — is the real ceiling on what a stranger can cost
# you. The per-visitor cap here is a signed cookie: clearing cookies resets it,
# which is an accepted trade (see the spec's "soft cap"). The circuit breaker
# stops one warm instance hammering an exhausted quota; it does not bound spend.
HOSTED_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Which provider serves hosted runs: "groq" or "gemini".
# Should be chosen by measurement, not preference — see
# docs/superpowers/notes/2026-08-24-live-provider-findings.md.
HOSTED_PROVIDER=groq

# HMAC secret for the free-run counter cookie. Must be at least 16 characters;
# anything shorter disables hosted runs rather than metering them insecurely.
# Generate one:
#   node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
FREE_RUN_SECRET=
